Open Racing Simulator — Robot Tutorial
======================================

This is the browser-based tutorial for developing robot drivers in Open Racing
Simulator (a community fork of TORCS).

To read the tutorial, open `index.html` in your browser.  The tutorial walks
through installing the simulator, setting up a build environment, and building
a robot driver step by step in C++.

The tutorial was originally written by Bernhard Wymann for TORCS.  The
underlying simulator API is largely unchanged, so the content remains
applicable.  Refer to `src/doc/architecture.md` in the repository root for
an up-to-date overview of the simulator's architecture.

For contributor setup instructions see `CONTRIBUTING.md` in the repository
root.

Have fun,

Bernhard Wymann.

